one issue I noticed is that we may add a `room` to `ctx.log_context_fields` it overwrites the value here, maybe we shouldn't overwrite the value in https://github.com/livekit/agents/blob/livekit-agents@1.3.5/livekit-agents/livekit/agents/job.py#L222?
```python
    ctx.log_context_fields = {
        "room": ctx.room.name,
    }
```

description:
Closes https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/5495 https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/635 https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/1510

I don't love this API but it's the best we've got at the moment. This is 100% opt-in. The classic `.optional()` will continue behaving as it always has. 

```ts
const A = z.object({
  a: z.string().optional(),
  b: z.string().exactOptional(),
});

type A = z.infer<typeof A>;
// => {
//   a?: string | undefined;
//   b?: string;
// }

A.parse({}); // ✅
A.parse({ a: undefined }); // ✅
A.parse({ b: undefined }); // ❌
```

Trying to enable exact optionality via some kind of global config is too kludgey and footgunny, so it needed to be an explicit API.

