human_review_comments.body:
@peterbud Thanks for the speedy feedback. I have understood (assumed, perhaps?) `tsql` dialect should support both SQL Server & Azure Synapse versions, alongside others listed by [T-SQL language reference](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/language-reference?view=sql-server-ver17).  I think this is the source of specification discrepancies.  

AFAIK you're correct SQL Server only supports one filepath, but Synapse (a) supports multiple paths and (b) where multiple filepaths are specified, requires brackets.  For reference info see [Synapse multiple filepaths](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/sql/query-folders-multiple-csv-files)

Let me know what you think or if you disagree with what I've mentioned regarding the dialect scope.

